:e
:re
// However, we cannot provide only part of the extraction parameters. The rule
// is that we either provide all of them or none at all.
if [0, 0] is P(Bit, a) then a
//│ ╔══[COMPILATION ERROR] Expected two extraction arguments, but found only one argument.
//│ ║  l.481: 	if [0, 0] is P(Bit, a) then a
//│ ╙──       	               ^^^^^^
//│ ═══[RUNTIME ERROR] Error: match error

:e
:re
// But `P` is not equivalent to `P'`! If no extraction parameters are declared,
// then none can be provided.
if [0, 0] is P'(Bit, a, b) then "values: " + a + ", " + b
//│ ╔══[COMPILATION ERROR] Expected zero extraction arguments, but found two arguments.
//│ ║  l.491: 	if [0, 0] is P'(Bit, a, b) then "values: " + a + ", " + b
//│ ╙──       	                ^^^^^^^^^
//│ ═══[RUNTIME ERROR] Error: match error

:fixme
// Order actually matters. But it seems that I didn't implement the error
// reporting correctly.
if [0, 0] is P(a, Bit, b) then "values: " + a + ", " + b
//│ ╔══[COMPILATION ERROR] No definition found in scope for member 'a'
//│ ║  l.500: 	if [0, 0] is P(a, Bit, b) then "values: " + a + ", " + b
//│ ╙──       	                                            ^
//│ ═══[RUNTIME ERROR] ReferenceError: a is not defined

